WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.680
Researchers have mapped how a single metabolite shields its own consuming enzyme from degradation signals in tryptophan metabolism. This is Planetarian Daily, episode 237. A closer look at that second binding site comes first, then microneedle delivery through skin, and fungal volatiles as chemistry for crops. Tryptophan takes up an allosteric pocket on the enzyme TDO2, according to Fizz.org coverage of a molecular cell paper from the Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.440
battery. Occupying that pocket keeps trip-to-fan breakdown at the right level, so the cell does

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.500
not burn through its own substrate. Groups at the University of Nevada, Las Vegas, and

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.300
the Dee-Doov Institute in Brussels joined that mapping. Something most people get wrong

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:48.440
is the idea that enzymes simply bind a metabolite and convert it until the substrate runs low,

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:54.780
with little internal feedback of their own. TDO2 and Trip-to-fan metabolism faces exactly

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.400
that risk, because the molecule it consumes is also the Q that should keep the pathway

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.040
in range.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:06.240
When TripDefense sits in the unexpected second location, it blocks access by the Kine-CK2

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.980
and the ubiquitin ligase CUL-1 beta-TRCP.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:12.860
That blockade stops a two-step markup.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:19.100
Phosphorylation first, then ubiquitination, the sequence that would tag TDO2 for destruction.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:24.360
The protective contact holds catabolism in balance without any outside signal arriving

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:29.580
at the cell. Break the allosteric contact and steady state levels of downstream metabolites

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:34.760
that influence inflammation and neurological function could shift. Mutating the second sight

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:39.360
while leaving the catalytic pocket intact is the experiment that would show how much of ordinary

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:45.550
metabolic control hangs on that single step. Micro-needle platforms now pair mechanical puncture

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:50.970
with controlled release for skin-targeted work, a review carried by Bioengineer.org finds.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:56.950
The same arrays can ferry nucleic acids for gene correction and present antigens for immunization.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:02.950
Fabrication now folds in sensors and materials that change their release when local conditions change.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:09.130
Preclinical results show tighter targeting of immune cells in the dermis than standard injection routes achieve.

00:02:10.027 --> 00:02:17.827
Toronto hosted the first animal longevity summit where scientists laid out gene therapies for canine heart disease and age-related muscle loss.

00:02:17.827 --> 00:02:24.627
The Portugal News reports, Rejuvenate Bio is testing a therapy for a common canine cardiac condition.

00:02:25.127 --> 00:02:28.927
Genflow biosciences is aiming at muscle preservation and older dogs.

00:02:29.447 --> 00:02:34.627
The Cat Health Company has two compounds in clinical trials for feline age-associated diseases.

00:02:35.127 --> 00:02:40.107
Money into these programs has risen as owners look for longer health spans and companion animals.

00:02:40.107 --> 00:02:47.510
Fungal volatile organic compounds cataloged over 20 years in a bioengineer.org review can

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:52.650
push plant growth, suppress pathogens, and serve as starting points for industrial chemicals.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:57.050
Species-specific volatile profiles now cover hundreds of isolates.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:02.130
Biofumigants and growth-promoting agents built from those profiles are meant to cut the

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:03.610
need for synthetic pesticides.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:09.570
The same body of work moves fungi out of the narrow roles of decomposer or pathogen and

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.490
and treats them as chemical signaling agents.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.980
Francis Crick Institute scientist found a specialized lipid layer in the fruit fly pupil

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:22.500
case that limits water loss when temperature is high and humidity is low, in a study covered

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.560
by Fizz.org.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.360
The barrier only holds so far, past its limit, survival falls off sharply.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:33.520
Those limits mean some insect populations may struggle to keep up with the hotter, drier

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.560
conditions climate projections describe.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:43.009
Uncrewed aircraft from a CIRS-led team now collect microplastic particles at different heights in the atmosphere.

00:03:43.549 --> 00:03:49.109
The method is meant to close gaps in how those particles travel long distances and settle in remote regions.

00:03:49.689 --> 00:03:54.789
Vertical profiles from the system can quantify transport routes that ground sampling cannot reach.

00:03:55.369 --> 00:04:05.934
Those results appear in scientific reports. Hong Kong University of Science and Technology President Nancy Ip received the UNESCO Equatorial Guinea International Prize for research

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:12.134
in the life sciences, the Detroit News reports. Her laboratory identified blood-based biomarkers

00:04:12.134 --> 00:04:16.734
that pick up Alzheimer's disease earlier than current clinical methods. The same tests

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:21.974
track progression over time and living patients. Her work runs from basic mechanisms of brain

00:04:21.974 --> 00:04:27.514
function through to translational diagnostic tools. The prize was presented in Paris on Friday.

00:04:28.613 --> 00:04:33.333
Engineers etched arrays of sub-wave length holes into silicon to make meta-surfaces that

00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:37.613
bend phase without swallowing ultraviolet light, according to Fizz.org.

00:04:38.093 --> 00:04:41.773
Those flat optics match focusing that used to need curved surfaces.

00:04:42.293 --> 00:04:47.173
The design is built for compact instruments that do high-resolution imaging and spectroscopy

00:04:47.173 --> 00:04:48.413
in the ultraviolet range.

00:04:49.425 --> 00:04:54.345
Kyushu University researchers built a packaging film that changes color and gives off fluorescence

00:04:54.345 --> 00:04:57.625
under ultraviolet light as spoilage compounds build up.

00:04:58.305 --> 00:05:03.225
Tests on refrigerated mutton produce both a visual cue and an optical readout as freshness

00:05:03.225 --> 00:05:09.565
declined. The film answers volatile molecules released while bacteria grow. Those results appeared

00:05:09.565 --> 00:05:15.052
in the chemical engineering journal. SinFIT scores candidate enzyme variants on several

00:05:15.052 --> 00:05:20.852
performance criteria at once, instead of chasing one property at a time. It steers directed

00:05:20.852 --> 00:05:26.552
evolution or computational design toward enzymes that hit industrial needs for activity, stability,

00:05:26.932 --> 00:05:31.972
and specificity together. That joint scoring cuts how many variants have to be synthesized

00:05:31.972 --> 00:05:37.684
and tested. An international collaboration built the first laboratory version of a three-component

00:05:37.684 --> 00:05:43.284
Hubbard model whose interaction strengths can be tuned. A quantum gas microscope imaged

00:05:43.284 --> 00:05:48.344
the individual atoms directly. The platform is set up for quantum simulations that matter

00:05:48.344 --> 00:05:54.824
to nuclear physics and to new materials. That work appears in science. Forest plots tuned for

00:05:54.824 --> 00:06:01.064
carbon storage often hold fewer species than plots managed first for habitat. A University of Copenhagen

00:06:01.064 --> 00:06:06.624
analysis finds. Carbon sequestration and species richness pull apart in space inside the

00:06:06.624 --> 00:06:11.924
same stands. Regional plans that want both outcomes have to give different ground to each goal,

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:18.323
rather than asking one stand to do both. From two other benches, nano particles drawn from milk

00:06:18.323 --> 00:06:24.383
carried gene therapy into bile duct cancer models in Mayo Clinic preclinical work. Penn State ran

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:29.643
an atom scale model of silicon carbide as it shifts from solid to vapor in crystal production,

00:06:29.643 --> 00:06:33.303
Trimming the need for trial and error in electronics manufacturing.

00:06:33.743 --> 00:06:39.603
Before we go, mutating TDO2's second site while the catalytic pocket stays intact is

00:06:39.603 --> 00:06:42.023
the next measurement that metabolism paper names.

